{
 "ep": 16,
 "total": 140,
 "title": "Create and Drop Databases Safely",
 "phase": "Installation & Administration",
 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "Creating a database is easy. Deleting one safely matters.",
   "cap": "*Creating* is easy. *Deleting* safely matters."
  },
  {
   "say": "This is episode sixteen of the PostgreSQL DBA series: create databases the right way, and drop them without surprises.",
   "cap": "Episode 16: *create* and *drop* databases.",
   "cue": "create"
  },
  {
   "say": "To create a database, you must be a superuser, or have the CREATEDB privilege.",
   "cap": "You need *superuser* or *CREATEDB.*",
   "cue": "superuser"
  },
  {
   "say": "A new database never starts empty. CREATE DATABASE clones a template, and by default that is template1.",
   "cap": "It *clones* a template. Default: *template1.*",
   "cue": "clones"
  },
  {
   "say": "So anything you add to template1 is copied into every new database made from it.",
   "cap": "Objects in *template1* are *copied* into new databases.",
   "cue": "copied"
  },
  {
   "say": "template0 holds only the standard objects of your PostgreSQL version. It should never be changed.",
   "cap": "*template0:* standard objects only. *Never* change it.",
   "cue": "never"
  },
  {
   "say": "Copy template0 when you need a new encoding or locale. A copy of template1 must keep its settings.",
   "cap": "New *encoding* or *locale?* Copy *template0.*",
   "cue": "encoding"
  },
  {
   "say": "Here is a real test. We create appdb, owned by app_user, from template0, with a connection limit of twenty.",
   "cap": "*appdb,* owner *app_user,* *template0,* limit *20.*",
   "cue": "create"
  },
  {
   "say": "pg_database shows the result. template0 has datallowconn set to false, so nobody can connect and change it.",
   "cap": "*template0:* datallowconn = *false.*",
   "cue": "false"
  },
  {
   "say": "First mistake: CREATE DATABASE cannot run inside a transaction block. We tried, and got exactly that error.",
   "cap": "*Not* inside a *transaction block.*",
   "cue": "transaction"
  },
  {
   "say": "Second mistake: copying a busy database. With one other session connected, it fails: source database is being accessed by other users.",
   "cap": "Busy template: *being accessed* by *other users.*",
   "cue": "fails"
  },
  {
   "say": "Now the dangerous part. DROP DATABASE removes the catalog entries and deletes the data directory. It cannot be undone.",
   "cap": "*DROP DATABASE* deletes the data. *No undo.*",
   "cue": "dangerous"
  },
  {
   "say": "Only the owner or a superuser can drop it, and never while connected to it. Connect to postgres first.",
   "cap": "*Owner* or *superuser,* from *another* database.",
   "cue": "connected"
  },
  {
   "say": "If anyone else is connected, the drop fails with the same error: being accessed by other users.",
   "cap": "Other sessions? The *drop fails.*",
   "cue": "fails"
  },
  {
   "say": "A safe sequence. First, ALTER DATABASE with ALLOW_CONNECTIONS false, so no new sessions can connect.",
   "cap": "Step 1: *ALLOW_CONNECTIONS false.*",
   "cue": "First"
  },
  {
   "say": "New logins now fail with: database is not currently accepting connections. Existing sessions keep running.",
   "cap": "New logins *refused.* Existing sessions *stay.*",
   "cue": "fail"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then DROP DATABASE WITH FORCE. It tries to terminate the existing connections, and here the drop succeeded.",
   "cap": "Step 2: *WITH (FORCE)* ends the sessions.",
   "cue": "FORCE"
  },
  {
   "say": "FORCE still fails if prepared transactions, active logical replication slots, or subscriptions are present.",
   "cap": "FORCE *fails* with prepared xacts, *slots,* subscriptions.",
   "cue": "fails"
  },
  {
   "say": "In scripts, IF EXISTS turns a missing database into a notice, instead of an error.",
   "cap": "*IF EXISTS:* a *notice,* not an error.",
   "cue": "notice"
  },
  {
   "say": "DBA takeaway, a common practice: take a fresh backup, check the name twice, and confirm nobody still needs it.",
   "cap": "*Backup* first, check the *name,* confirm with *owners.*",
   "cue": "backup"
  },
  {
   "say": "Recap: new databases clone template1 by default. Use template0 for a clean copy, or a new encoding.",
   "cap": "Recap: *template1* default, *template0* for clean.",
   "cue": "template0"
  },
  {
   "say": "No transaction blocks, no busy templates, block connections before a drop, and remember: a drop is permanent.",
   "cap": "*Block* connections, then *drop.* It's *permanent.*",
   "cue": "block"
  },
  {
   "say": "Next up: schemas and the search path. Follow so you don't miss it, and send this to a friend who's learning PostgreSQL.",
   "cap": "Next up: *schemas* and *search_path.* *Follow* and share."
  }
 ],
